      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coldenham%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original Coldenham farmhouse, once home to Cadwallader Colden Jr. and his wife Anna, still stands today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/coldenham/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before the American Revolution, the Colden family owned vast tracts of land across New York, cementing their regional influence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/coldenham/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Coldenham sits 440 feet above sea level, offering modest elevation within the rolling hills of Orange County.",
